This is the audited dirty-source manifest for the release candidate. Each line is a SHA-256 of the exact candidate working-tree byte stream followed by two spaces and its repository-relative path. Git blob hashes may differ for text files because Git's configured line-ending normalization applies when objects are staged; binaries retain their byte identity. The isolated candidate was copied from the shared checkout and every selected source hash matched both immediately before and after copy; all paths below were rehashed at capture.

Included: 76 modified/untracked runtime, required production-atlas, and regression-test paths. The committed beta baseline also carries seven commits ahead of main, including clinical content whose existing review status/provenance remains unchanged; this capture does not promote draft content.

Excluded from the dirty workspace: screenshots/review artifacts, GS-013 character-fitting experiments and mappings, private/ignored clinical and photo inputs, generated source art, ComfyUI inputs, disposable tooling artifacts, unrelated documents and plans. The changed founder atlas generator/verifiers are excluded because production Pages builds use the committed atlas PNGs and manifest directly; source regeneration depends on excluded development-only inputs. The changed browser regression `tests/e2e/character-resolution-zoom.spec.ts` is included.

